notes.body:
I had a closer look and I don't think this requires a new dissector. It's just a port for SOAP over UDP.

Try this patch. What else do you need to decode WS-Discovery?

```
diff --git a/epan/dissectors/packet-xml.c b/epan/dissectors/packet-xml.c
index 5391561384..c4c7413866 100644
--- a/epan/dissectors/packet-xml.c
+++ b/epan/dissectors/packet-xml.c
@@ -1548,6 +1548,7 @@ proto_reg_handoff_xml(void)
 {
     wmem_map_foreach(media_types, add_dissector_media, NULL);
     dissector_add_uint_range_with_preference("tcp.port", "", xml_handle);
+    dissector_add_uint_range_with_preference("udp.port", "", xml_handle);

     heur_dissector_add("http",  dissect_xml_heur, "XML in HTTP", "xml_http", xml_ns.hf_tag, HEURISTIC_DISABLE);
     heur_dissector_add("sip",   dissect_xml_heur, "XML in SIP", "xml_sip", xml_ns.hf_tag, HEURISTIC_DISABLE);```
